			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> The young East Asian woman from reference image 1. Preserve her facial identity, short layered black hair with soft bangs, natural youthful facial proportions, realistic skin texture, and black satin short-sleeve pajama set with white piping.\n\n<Subject 2> The young East Asian woman from reference image 2. Preserve her facial identity, round metal-frame glasses, loosely tied black hair with natural stray strands, beige oversized knitted sweater, loose cream trousers, and understated natural appearance.\n\n<Picture 1> The rainy old-city bus stop from reference image 3. Preserve the glass-and-metal shelter, metal bench, wet asphalt, reflective puddles, old low-rise buildings, scattered fallen leaves, distant shop lights, street lamps, rain-soaked road surface, and lonely late-night urban atmosphere.\n\n\nsummary:\nA 10-second live-action melancholic emotional drama at a rainy bus stop late at night. Two women share a restrained farewell conversation. The sequence focuses on facial performance, hesitation, eye contact, emotional distance, and the final physical separation rather than exaggerated crying. The visual language is intimate and cinematic, beginning with close emotional coverage and gradually opening the space only after the relationship changes.\n\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved for facial identity, hairstyle, body proportions, skin appearance, and black satin pajama outfit.\n\n<Subject 2>: fully_preserved for facial identity, round glasses, hairstyle, body proportions, beige knitwear outfit, and natural appearance.\n\n<Picture 1>: fully_preserved for the rainy bus stop architecture, wet road, old-city surroundings, practical lights, reflective pavement, metal bench, shelter glass, and nighttime atmosphere. Character blocking is added without redesigning the environment.\n\n\ndetailed_description:\nLive-action melancholic urban drama with restrained, natural performance. The entire scene takes place under steady nighttime rain. Preserve realistic skin texture, damp hair strands, slightly humid fabric, believable rain interaction, natural wet-surface reflections, and subtle environmental moisture.\n\nThe overall exposure is slightly lowered. Cool blue-gray ambient light from the rainy street forms the main visual base. Small distant warm shop lights and weak street lamps create muted amber reflections on the wet pavement and shelter glass. Skin tones remain natural and are not heavily tinted. Keep moderate shallow depth of field during close shots, then gradually allow more spatial information to become readable in the final continuous shot.\n\nThe emotional staging must use depth rather than flat side-by-side placement. <Subject 1> remains deeper inside the shelter. <Subject 2> stays closer to the open end of the shelter and the rainy street, already physically positioned as if preparing to leave. They do not stand directly face-to-face in a flat line.\n\n[Shot 1]\n0.0-2.8s.\n\nClose-up of <Subject 1> from slightly off her frontal axis, showing a natural three-quarter facial angle.\n\nShe stands inside the shelter near a rain-covered glass panel. A softly blurred vertical edge of the shelter structure occupies a small portion of the foreground, creating subtle visual separation.\n\n<Subject 2> is only faintly visible as a soft out-of-focus human shape deeper behind her near the shelter exit.\n\nThe camera begins already close and moves forward only a very small amount, extremely slowly.\n\n<Subject 1> keeps her body mostly still. She first looks toward <Subject 2> with restrained hesitation. Her lips press together slightly. She takes a shallow breath, waits a brief moment, then speaks quietly.\n\n(S1) says <d>[Chinese]你真的要走吗？</d>\n\nAfter speaking, she does not look away. She keeps watching <Subject 2>, waiting.\n\nRain striking the shelter roof remains clearly audible beneath her voice.\n\n\n[Shot 2]\n2.8-5.6s.\n\nCut to a matching close-up of <Subject 2> from the same side of the interaction axis.\n\nKeep a similar subject size, similar camera height, similar perspective, and similar depth-of-field language to the previous shot.\n\nHer body is already angled slightly toward the rainy street, while only her head remains turned back toward <Subject 1>.\n\nThe blurred dark edge of <Subject 1>'s shoulder may remain faintly in the near foreground, preserving their spatial relationship.\n\nThe camera stays nearly fixed, with only minimal natural breathing drift.\n\n<Subject 2> looks at <Subject 1> for a brief moment without speaking.\n\nHer eyes then lower slightly behind the glasses.\n\nHer mouth opens a little, pauses, closes once, then opens again.\n\nShe takes a restrained breath and answers softly.\n\n(S2) says <d>[Chinese]再不走，我就舍不得了。</d>\n\nThe last few words become quieter.\n\nAfter speaking, she lowers her gaze and begins to turn her attention toward the shelter exit.\n\n\n[Shot 3]\n5.6-10.0s.\n\nCut to a two-person medium-close composition from the same camera side.\n\nDo not jump directly to a wide shot.\n\nBoth characters now appear together in the same frame for the first time.\n\n<Subject 1> remains deeper inside the shelter, closer to the glass panel and bench area.\n\n<Subject 2> stands closer to the open shelter edge and the rainy street.\n\nThey occupy different depth planes rather than standing evenly side by side.\n\nThe empty metal bench and part of the shelter structure remain visually between them, creating natural separation without blocking either face.\n\nAt the beginning of this shot, the framing is still relatively tight, keeping both women emotionally readable.\n\n<Subject 2> slowly turns her body away from <Subject 1>.\n\nShe pauses briefly after turning.\n\nThen she takes her first slow steps toward the rain.\n\nThe camera does not cut again.\n\nAs <Subject 2> moves away, the camera very slowly pulls backward by a small amount.\n\nThis gradual pull-back naturally changes the framing from a two-person medium-close shot into a wider medium shot.\n\nThe widening happens continuously inside the same shot rather than through a sudden cut.\n\n<Subject 1> remains completely still.\n\nShe does not follow, does not call out, and does not reach toward <Subject 2>.\n\n<Subject 2> gradually becomes smaller as she moves toward the rainy street.\n\nThe physical distance between the two women increases naturally.\n\nThe wet pavement, reflective puddles, bus shelter structure, empty bench, and dark abandoned umbrella near the curb gradually become more visible as the camera pulls back.\n\nDuring the final second, <Subject 1> is still standing under the shelter, watching <Subject 2> leave.\n\nHer shoulders lose a small amount of tension.\n\nHer eyes slowly lower.\n\nNo further dialogue.\n\nHold the unresolved emotional silence until the end.\n\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous realistic nighttime rainfall with layered spatial depth. Nearby rain strikes the shelter roof and glass panels with a clear metallic and glass resonance. Water drips steadily from the shelter edge. Rain falling across the open road sounds softer and more diffuse. Occasional distant vehicle tires move through wet pavement, creating low soft splashes.\n\nDialogue remains naturally embedded in the rainy environment and should not sound studio-dry.\n\nDuring each spoken line, irrelevant distant environmental sounds become slightly quieter while rain remains present.\n\nAfter the second line, dialogue disappears completely.\n\nThe final section is carried by rain, faint breathing, soft footfalls moving away from the shelter, water splashes under <Subject 2>'s steps, and distant wet-road ambience.\n\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nVery sparse melancholic piano begins only after <Subject 2> finishes her line, around 5.6 seconds.\n\nUse isolated soft piano notes with long decay and large silent spaces between them.\n\nThe music remains extremely low in volume and blends into the rain rather than dominating it.\n\nNo swelling strings, no dramatic crescendo, no sentimental melody, no emotional climax.\n\nThe final sound remains primarily rain and distance."
